{{addvar::hop7_emit_core::
<tool_schema>
{
  "name": "cast_voice",
  "displayName": "🎭 Cast & Voice",
  "description": "State type: Conditional. Job: Condition Check. Scope: Character. When: Before.\nEmit Cast & Voice only for a model-controlled new/returning participant or a material participation/voice change. Never emit this tool for the user-controlled character; the user owns their voice, actions and interiority. Read unchanged model-controlled profiles silently without reprinting them. No row for everyone mentioned in the setting. Preserve aliases and distinguish namesakes with a short role suffix.\nEvery model-controlled spoken-language participant with a Cast & Voice record has a concrete accent/performance profile. General American English is a concrete option; accentless, neutral, no clear regional origin, or timbre-only labels are not. A newly assigned compatible accent is a creative continuity choice, not a claim about canon or nationality.\nFor signed, written-only or nonverbal communication omit Accent; do not pretend these people must speak. Keep their actual communication style in the scene.\nNever emit Cast & Voice for a User-controlled character. Read the user character only through supplied user text, Turn Reading and explicit OOC direction; never manufacture a user voice profile.\nA quiet participant can observe or be affected. Elsewhere and Only mentioned permit an empty Participation list, not telepathic attendance.\nRead prior named Cast & Voice results in supplied history. No C01 codes, speaking-order identities, source token counts or hidden character-number fields.\nWhen a recorded model-controlled character speaks, realize the retained voice in the actual line. Use a stable mixture of syntax, diction, idiom, contractions, conversational habits, cadence, and restrained phonetic spelling where useful. Code-switching is not a default accent marker and should appear only when already established or naturally motivated. Speaker attribution must not be the only thing distinguishing voices; a recurring line should usually be identifiable without its speaker label. Avoid phonetic caricature and do not distort every word.\nElsewhere and Only mentioned require an empty Participation list; they cannot hold a current scene role or gain telepathic attendance. A quiet participant who is actually Present can still observe or be affected.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "character": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "🎭 Character",
        "description": "Use the existing character name. Establish a clear identifying name for a genuinely new participant. Reference source: cast. New subject: Only when establishing a genuinely new named subject.",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 96
      },
      "played_by": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "👑 Played by",
        "description": "Cast & Voice is emitted only for model-controlled characters.",
        "minLength": 1,
        "enum": ["Model"]
      },
      "presence": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "📍 Presence",
        "description": "Where is this person now?",
        "minLength": 1,
        "enum": ["Here", "Remote through an established channel", "Elsewhere", "Only mentioned"]
      },
